//
// Inputs and outputs of the relation evaluations (`RelationsLib`) of the reference
// verifier: the Solidity verifier that Barretenberg 6.0.0 writes for `vectors/vk` with
// `bb write_solidity_verifier -t evm` (sha256 of the generated file
// 5609d13dbb405085cff8ba549254f73dfdc3677edbe391a4a73174d3878d8bfe), compiled with
// solc 0.8.34 (optimizer_runs = 1, evm_version = osaka) and run with forge 1.5.1.
//
// How captured: a local, untracked Foundry harness that inherits the generated
// `HonkVerifier` calls its ten `accumulate*Relation` functions, in the order of
// `accumulateRelationEvaluations`, on one shared array, then
// `scaleAndBatchSubrelations` and `accumulateRelationEvaluations` itself, and writes
// the values below. The harness also checked that both batching entry points agree,
// that each relation run alone on a zeroed array writes exactly its own slots, that
// every captured subrelation is reduced (< P), and that `PROOF_BATCHED` satisfies the
// final equation of the reference's `verifySumcheck` for the pinned proof while
// `PROOF_BATCHED_TAMPERED` does not.
//
// Two input sets:
//
// - `PROOF_*`: what `verifySumcheck` hands to the relations for the pinned proof
//   `vectors/proof` (sha256 7ff3d7402d792648e68b8aa359b27a16322859b5d1c44eb45ff36d135ad96553)
//   with `vectors/public_inputs`: sumcheck evaluations 1..41, the relation parameters
//   (with the public-input delta), alpha, and the partial pow after the last round. The
//   circuit only has arithmetic gates, so 13 entity evaluations are zero (the lookup
//   selector and table columns, q_r, q_4 and the six selectors after q_arith) and only
//   subrelations 0..7 are non-zero: this set alone cannot tell a correct range, elliptic,
//   memory, ROM, non-native-field or Poseidon2 term from a wrong one.
// - `SYNTH_*`: pseudo-random inputs, so that every entity and all 31 subrelations are
//   non-zero. Input `i` is the keccak256 hash of the ASCII bytes of
//   `ultrahonk-relations-synthetic` followed by `i` as a 32-byte big-endian word, reduced
//   mod P: i = 0..40 the entities, 41 eta, 42 romLogupGamma, 43 beta, 44 gamma,
//   45 publicInputsDelta, 46 alpha, 47 the partial pow. The reference received
//   `alphas[k] = alpha^(k+1)`, the shape its transcript produces.
//
// `*_BATCHED_TAMPERED` is the batched result after adding one to the evaluation of entity
// `TAMPERED_ENTITY` (`W_L`), everything else unchanged.

